{"name":"Farina","hex":"#dfc38d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Farina","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Italian."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Farina"}],"entries":[{"title":"Farina, South Australia","blocks":[{"text":"Farina, formerly Farina Town and originally Government Gums, is an abandoned town in the Australian state of South Australia. The name also applies to an area of about 8500 square kilometres in which the town is located. At the 2006 census, 55 people lived in the larger area; by the 2021 census, the population had fallen to 15."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Farina_sign.jpg/330px-Farina_sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farina%2C_South_Australia","wikidata":"Q5435313"},{"title":"Farina, Illinois","blocks":[{"text":"Farina is a village in Fayette and Marion counties, Illinois, United States. The population was 540 at the 2020 census. It is the only community with the name \"Farina\" in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Marion_County_Illinois_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Farina_Highlighted.svg/330px-Marion_County_Illinois_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Farina_Highlighted.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farina%2C_Illinois","wikidata":"Q2608106"},{"title":"Farina (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Farina or Fariña is a surname, meaning flour in several Romance languages. Notable people with the surname include:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farina_(surname)","wikidata":"Q16869896"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Farina_cemetery.jpg/500px-Farina_cemetery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikime